{"kind":"request","text":"From Hugh, 2026-10-04: Write the composable authority-scope and GitHub demonstration design. Start with wavelet-like scopes as a primitive expression of authority boundaries. Make lane the concrete model for gitseq-style work as it happens: issue/goal, requests and commitments, discussion, splitting concerns, contribution, evidence and recombination into an exact proposed-and-mergeable deployable change. Issues and PRs are specific lane forms. The demo should reproduce GitHub's user experience as closely as reasonably possible, adding a coherent view of the work that bridges issue/goal and PR. Production rollout of deployable changes is expressly outside this design. I am preparing an initial architecture draft in plans/017-2026-10-04-composable-lanes-and-github-demo.md for planner to reconcile, obtain independent review and turn into concrete design/proof/implementation tasks. Preserve existing owed work and current implementation priorities until a separate priority decision.","body":{"conditions":"A self-contained design draft and planner task map start from composable authority scopes. A lane is the durable work-as-it-happens model that transforms an issue or goal into a proposed and mergeable result; issue and PR discussions are lane forms, not adjacent objects with a separate execution-only lane. Specify splitting concerns, multiple contributors and recombination into one exact deployable change; preserve individual provenance and qualified review. Target an exact-as-reasonable clone of the GitHub user experience with a reviewable parity matrix and bounded distributed-scope validation scenarios. Keep pushing deployable changes into production, rollout, promotion and production recovery outside this design. Reconcile existing D1/N2, proposal reads, browser/runtime, declared acts, collections and documentation work, recording owners, remaining decisions, dependencies and bounded acceptance evidence. New architecture remains proposed until reviewed/adopted; no source implementation or reprioritization is implied by commissioning this design.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}